   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<ol class=\"os-raise-noindent\" start=\"5\">\n    <li>Shannon is running on a flat, rocky trail that eventually rises up a steep mountain. The graph below represents the total distance she covers with respect to time. <br> <br> <img src=\"exercises/media/a877f1d48c6e24d9.jpg\" width=\"300\" alt=\"A line graph showing total distance in miles on the vertical axis and time in minutes on the horizontal axis. An orange curve starts at zero minutes and zero miles, increasing as time progresses from 0 to 60 minutes. The rate of increase gradually decreases over time, reaching approximately 3 miles at the 60 minute mark.\"></li>\n    </ol><p>How many miles does Shannon run in 60 minutes?&nbsp;</p>",
